ive eating  will cause you to lose weight I'm just  saying for this process to work and it  is a process we need to put those  thoughts and those tools on the back  burner and that way we can really focus  on rebuilding a trustful relationship  with our bodies and food and finally  that brings me to step number 4 be  compassionate to yourself as you move  forward in this life diet free you're  probably going to be tempted to be  pulled back into diet culture remember  it is everywhere so this is totally  normal so if you're scrolling through  Instagram and you get the feeling or  thought that you want to go on a diet  don't beat yourself up about it  I mean take a minute to think about why  that photo or program or copy or blog  post or whatever incited this thought  also think about whether or not you're  ready to put the restrictive diets on  the back burner right now and if you  think that this is really the best thing  to do both for your physical and mental  health right now remember no judgement  for me we really all have to come into  this when we're ready intuitive eating  takes time and patience you're going to  have setbacks it's inevitable but take  these setbacks as learning up shinee's  rather than failures now if you're  wondering if you're falling back into  diet mentality or how to even identify  diet mentality I want to share a few  really important comparisons that we're  in the intuitive eating book that might  help you along in your journey for  eating and food choices diet talk sounds  like do I deserve it  eating is going to make me feel bad that  food is bad for me that food is good for  me I'm eating clean  in comparison non-diet talk sounds like  am i hungry do I want to eat it am I in  the mood for it  will I be deprived if I don't have it  will it taste good I deserve to enjoy  eating food without feeling any guilt  when it comes to exercise diet talk  sounds like I want to burn as many  calories as possible if I miss a workout  I'm gonna feel bad if I workout for just  another hour then I can work off that  doughnut that I ate earlier  comparatively non diet talk sounds like  exercising makes me feel happy I feel  strong and energized after my workouts  I'm less stress after working out okay  so now that you know the four steps in  the first principle to reject the diet  mentality I want to give you your weekly  exercise so what you're gonna work on  this week is you're gonna clean up your  social media feeds scroll through your  feed and pay attention to diet mentality  so words like clean eating or good food  bad food comparisons or need to earn  your meal or cheat days all of that  should be flagged start to really tune  in to this language and ask yourself how  it feels to see this language and read  this copy or see these images now that  you're trying to think about food and  more  morally neutral terms so if it doesn't  feel like it works for you anymore  unfollow or unsubscribe and fill your  feets with people who have more  supportive relationships with food  remember that intuitive eating is all  about respecting your body's natural  signals and desires  now intuitive eating does fall short and  its ability to describe how trauma  impacts our relationship with food and  our bodies so if this is something that  you were struggling with definitely  reach out to a licensed therapist to get  the support that you need  in the meantime continue to follow at  the intuitive eating series our next  principle is on your hunger so stay  tuned for that if you like this video be  sure to give it a thumbs up leave me a  comment below with any of your questions  related to intuitive eating pays body  positivity etc I will always be making a  running list and I'm gonna be answering  one of those main questions every single  video here subscribe to the channel and  I will see you next time on Abby's  kitchen bye  [Music]  [Music]
 

